    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear offensive anchor; his 82.97 efficiency score is fueled by an elite 0.474 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (5.28 xERA). Alongside him, **Caleb Durbin** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** are priority starts. **Caleb Durbin** (70.29) benefits significantly from facing Jacob Lopez, whose slow delivery provides the exact environment we crave to capitalize on our scarcity-driven SB focus. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.56) earns his spot at the top of the order; while the matchup against Dustin May is stiffer, his 10% order bonus and the high-leverage environment make him an essential engine for our Roto categories. **Trea Turner** rounds out the elite tier (68.26), as his ability to weaponize the 88% SB delivery rate of his opposing pitcher outweighs the moderate skill of the starter.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer involved **Carson Benge**, who finished just outside the starting cut with a 35.80 score. While **Carson Benge** offers upside, his production is suppressed today by a brutal pairing with Chris Sale (3.04 xERA) and an elevated 45% rain risk, which ultimately forced us to favor the matchup consistency of **Nelson Velazquez** and **Lars Nootbaar**. We continue to monitor the status of **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** against Trevor Rogers; both are currently projected for solid mid-50s scores due to the platoon advantage, but any late-inning defensive substitutions for **Colt Keith**\u2014a perennial risk given the lefty-on-lefty suppression\u2014could shrink our efficiency margins. We are also keeping a close watch on **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains rostered but unavailable in the Oklahoma City Comets system, as well as depth pieces like **Casey Schmitt**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, who remain in reserve as we navigate the remaining game caps. Owners should also note that **Kyle Schwarber** remains sidelined, necessitating a reliance on **Gary Sanchez** to provide the necessary power floor at C2 despite a difficult matchup against Logan Webb.",
